  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Leidos has federal contract obligations of $2B for FY2026 to date. Leidos recorded 2,777 awards with an average award size of $730K. Obligations fell 33.3% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer of Leidos services, obligating $1.5B. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $233M and the Department of Transportation obligated $131M. Leidos’s work concentrates in technology and services markets. Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $641M and Computer Facilities Management Services accounts for $556M. Electronic Computer Manufacturing accounts for $307M and Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance accounts for $227M. Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services shows $131M and Engineering Services shows $63.2M. Historical obligations show FY21 at $1.9B, FY22 at $2.7B, FY23 at $2.6B, FY24 at $3B, FY25 at $3B, and FY26 at $2B. The General Services Administration shows $79.5M and the Department of Health and Human Services shows $50.9M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Leidos’s obligations by agency?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.5B. The Department of Homeland Security and the Department of Transportation follow at $233M and $131M respectively. Other buying agencies include the General Services Administration at $79.5M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $50.9M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets drive Leidos’s federal work?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services and Computer Facilities Management Services lead at $641M and $556M. Electronic Computer Manufacturing and Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance follow at $307M and $227M. Other notable markets include Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $131M and Engineering Services at $63.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
